From: nuno407 <11352538+nuno407@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 12:14:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 24/45] drm/tegra: gem: skip CPU cache maintenance when pinning
 native BOs

tegra_bo_pin() maps the BO for the client device with dma_map_sgtable()
on every pin, and the legacy job submission path (DRM_TEGRA_SUBMIT, used
by the grate/opentegra GLES driver) pins every buffer of every job. On a
non-coherent ARM SoC this cleans the whole BO from L1/L2 each time: with
a 1366x768 colour + depth target that is several MiB of cache cleaning
per draw call. perf on a Tegra30 shows 90% of a kmscube process in
v7_dma_clean_range/l2c210_clean_range under tegra_bo_pin.

Native tegra BOs are only accessed by the CPU through write-combined
mappings (userspace mmap, kernel vmap and dma_alloc_wc all use WC) and
their pages are flushed when they are allocated, so there is nothing to
clean or invalidate. Pass DMA_ATTR_SKIP_CPU_SYNC for them. Imported
dma-bufs keep using the exporter's map/unmap and are unaffected.
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/tegra/gem.c | 14 ++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/tegra/gem.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/tegra/gem.c
index 436394e04..1608b7edf 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/tegra/gem.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/tegra/gem.c
@@ -129,7 +129,16 @@ static struct host1x_bo_mapping *tegra_bo_pin(struct device *dev, struct host1x_
 			goto free;
 	}
 
-	err = dma_map_sgtable(dev, map->sgt, direction, 0);
+	/*
+	 * Native buffer objects are only ever accessed by the CPU through
+	 * write-combined mappings (userspace mmap, kernel vmap, dma_alloc_wc),
+	 * and their pages were flushed from the caches when they were
+	 * allocated. Cache maintenance on every pin is therefore pointless, and
+	 * very expensive: legacy job submissions pin every BO of every job, so
+	 * a 1366x768 render target cost ~4 MiB of cache cleaning per draw call
+	 * on Tegra30 (90% of the CPU time of a GLES client in perf).
+	 */
+	err = dma_map_sgtable(dev, map->sgt, direction, DMA_ATTR_SKIP_CPU_SYNC);
 	if (err)
 		goto free_sgt;
 
@@ -165,7 +174,8 @@ static void tegra_bo_unpin(struct host1x_bo_mapping *map)
 						  map->direction);
 		dma_buf_detach(map->attach->dmabuf, map->attach);
 	} else {
-		dma_unmap_sgtable(map->dev, map->sgt, map->direction, 0);
+		dma_unmap_sgtable(map->dev, map->sgt, map->direction,
+				  DMA_ATTR_SKIP_CPU_SYNC);
 		sg_free_table(map->sgt);
 		kfree(map->sgt);
 	}
